ntains detailed information on traffic)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 365.70 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (accidents in 2016, comprising 45 variables across 124,992 records. The analysis began with a comprehensive)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 353.03 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (exploration of the data, identifying key variables and relationships through statistical checks, filtering data, and)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 340.36 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (investigating patterns across measures and categories.)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 316.11 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (Findings indicate that Zuid-Holland and Noord-Holland experience the highest number of accidents, primarily in)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 303.44 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (urban areas due to higher traffic density and congestion. Geospatial analytics played a key role in uncovering these)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 290.77 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (insights by analyzing the location component of the data.)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 278.10 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (Additionally, the analysis reveals that straight roads account for the majority of accidents, likely due to speeding and)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 265.43 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (driver inattention. Zuid-Holland records the highest number of casualties \(5,611\), highlighting the urgent need for)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 252.76 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (targeted safety measures in these provinces.)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 228.51 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (Accidents are most frequent during rush hour \(5€6 PM\) and peak on Thursdays and Fridays, coinciding with end-of-)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 215.84 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (week commuting. May and September show notable increases in accidents and casualties, with these months also)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 203.17 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (recording the highest casualty-to-accident ratios, suggesting more severe incidents. A significant proportion of)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 190.50 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (accidents \(33.5%\) involve uninsured drivers, and passenger cars are the most common vehicles involved \(91%\).)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 177.83 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (Adults aged 31€60 are most affected, with Thursdays and Fridays showing heightened risks for this group. Though)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 165.16 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (less frequent, accidents involving older adults and children demand focused interventions, such as safer road)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 152.49 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (designs and targeted education.)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 128.24 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (Side collisions dominate accident types, especially at 4-way crossings, while straight roads account for the highest)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 115.57 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (overall accident counts. Most accidents occur under dry weather conditions, with material-only damage comprising)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 102.90 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (80% of incidents. However, 63.71% of casualties require hospital treatment, highlighting the severity of many)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 90.23 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (accidents.)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 65.97 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (To improve road safety, recommendations include enhancing road design, increasing law enforcement presence,)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 53.31 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (and running targeted awareness campaigns focusing on high-risk areas, times, and behaviors. Seasonal spikes in)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 40.64 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (May and September require proactive traffic management and driver education programs. For insurance claims,)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 27.97 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (validating accident details against identified patterns, such as road type, time, and location, can improve accuracy)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 15.30 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (and fraud detection. This report presents actionable insights to reduce accidents, prioritize safety measures, and)Tj ET Q q /GS0 gs 0.165 0.188 0.216 RG 0.165 0.188 0.216 rg BT 0.00 2.63 Td /TT0 10.34 Tf (support data-driven decision-making in traffic management and insurance.)Tj ET Q Q Q Q Q q 23.52 254.88 528.96 455.04 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 24.00 255.36 cm Q Q q 23.52 254.88 528.96 455.04 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 24.00 255.36 cm Q Q q 23.52 254.88 528.96 455.04 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 24.00 255.36 cm Q Q q 3.36 734.88 569.28 17.28 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 3.84 735.36 cm q -0.48 -0.48 569.28 17.28 re W* n q /GS0 gs 0.000 0.000 0.000 RG 0.000 0.000 0.000 rg BT 226.56 3.43 Td /TT0 13.50 Tf (Executive Summary)Tj ET Q Q Q Q q 3.36 734.88 569.28 17.28 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 3.84 735.36 cm Q Q q 3.36 734.88 569.28 17.28 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 3.84 735.36 cm Q Q q 3.36 734.88 569.28 17.28 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 3.84 735.36 cm Q Q q 284.16 3.36 7.20 15.36 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 284.64 3.84 cm q -0.48 -0.48 7.20 15.36 re W* n q /GS0 gs 0.000 0.000 0.000 RG 0.000 0.000 0.000 rg BT 0.00 3.05 Td /TT0 12.00 Tf (1)Tj ET Q Q Q Q q 284.16 3.36 7.20 15.36 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 284.64 3.84 cm Q Q q 284.16 3.36 7.20 15.36 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 284.64 3.84 cm Q Q q 284.16 3.36 7.20 15.36 re W* n q 1 0 0 1 284.64 3.84 cm Q Q Q 
